WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.523
This video explains the comprehension ladder.

00:00:02.523 --> 00:00:06.007
It is a skill that helps a person understand something.

00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:11.235
The skill has four rungs. Prose, a diagram, a web page, and a video.

00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:13.480
This video is rung four.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.710
You ask a question. The skill reads your words and picks a rung.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.212
It also picks a strictness.

00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:23.673
The default is eighty percent of the way to Simplified Technical English.

00:00:23.673 --> 00:00:25.653
Strictness sets the sentence limit.

00:00:25.653 --> 00:00:29.504
At eighty percent, a sentence has twenty five words or fewer.

00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:33.154
Before it makes anything, the skill writes one outline.

00:00:33.154 --> 00:00:36.740
Claims, mechanism, hedges, and one real example.

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.442
Every rung shows that same outline. When you climb, the form changes.

00:00:41.442 --> 00:00:43.478
The facts stay the same.

00:00:43.478 --> 00:00:45.156
Rule one. Keep every hedge.

00:00:45.156 --> 00:00:50.962
If the source says "may be caused by a race condition", the skill keeps the word "may".

00:00:50.962 --> 00:00:57.113
Rule two. Add no facts. If a diff does not say why, the explanation says so.

00:00:57.113 --> 00:01:02.572
A linter checks the text. It finds long sentences, semicolons and marketing words.

00:01:02.572 --> 00:01:04.503
It never flags a hedge.

00:01:04.503 --> 00:01:07.466
A video needs a voice, a renderer and ffmpeg.

00:01:07.466 --> 00:01:10.500
The skill uses the first voice it finds.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:15.632
If Manim is not installed, a small renderer draws each frame with numpy and Pillow.

00:01:15.632 --> 00:01:17.824
This video was made that way.

00:01:17.824 --> 00:01:22.181
The linter checks form only. It cannot tell if an explanation is true.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:25.194
The outline and the two rules do that job.

00:01:25.194 --> 00:01:29.035
So pick a rung, keep the facts, and climb when you need more.
